# promise.reg - OpenSLP static service registration for VessApp / WebPAM PROe.
#
# Install as /etc/slp.reg and run OpenSLP `slpd` (the Linux replacement for the
# Windows slpreg.exe + slp.dll path invoked by slpreg.bat's `slpreg -once`).
# WebPAM's slp.php just start/stop/scopes the local SA; slp.dll strings confirm
# the OpenSLP framing this uses: service:service-agent, service:directory-agent,
# net.slp.useScopes.
#
# UNRESOLVED: the exact Promise vendor srvtype string registered by slp.dll on
# the box is not in any shipped artifact. Below we register the WebPAM
# management endpoint under a port-chosen type; confirm the real srvtype
# on-device with `slptool findsrvtypes` and substitute it here (CALIBRATE).
#
# Format (OpenSLP slp.reg):  service-url,language,lifetime  then attr=value lines.

service:vessapp.promise://vess-a3120.local:8443,en,65535
model=Vess A3120
description=Promise VessApp WebPAM PROe management
